# Databases (Prisma / SQLite)
#
# The -wal and -shm files matter as much as the database itself: SQLite in WAL
# mode keeps recently written rows in `lab.sqlite-wal`, not in `lab.sqlite`. A
# rule that caught only the main file would leave the most recent patients —
# the ones not yet checkpointed — sitting in a committable file.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sqlite-journal
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
prisma/migrations/migration_lock.toml.bak

# Certificates / signing keys (never commit)
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12

# Local launcher scripts (never commit)
#
# `.env` is ignored, so keys tend to end up in the next most convenient place
# instead: a double-clickable .cmd or .ps1 that sets them and starts something.
# That has already happened once in the folder above this repo, with a live
# Telegram token and two live LLM keys sitting in plaintext. Any launcher that
# carries a key belongs in a *-local file, and *-local is ignored.
*-local.cmd
*-local.ps1
*-local.bat
*-local.sh
secrets.*
*.secrets.*

# Database dumps (never commit)
# The nightly cloud backup is downloaded and decrypted into whatever directory
# you happen to be standing in, and the plaintext is every patient record the
# lab holds. Both the encrypted artifact and the decrypted dump are ignored so
# a restore performed inside the repo cannot end up in a commit.
*.sql.gpg
*.dump
backup*.sql
SHA256SUMS.txt

# Next.js generated route types (regenerated on every dev/build)
.next/types/
**/next-env.d.ts.bak

# Editor state
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Claude Code — machine-local permissions and settings. `settings.json` is the
# shared, committed one; `settings.local.json` is per-machine and must not be.
# Globbed rather than rooted: an app folder can carry its own .claude/, and the
# rooted rule silently missed those.
**/.claude/settings.local.json
**/.claude/local/

# Agent-runner scaffolding. These are workspace wrappers around the repo, not
# part of it — an OpenClaw clone in particular is several GB of checkout that
# has no business in a commit.
.openclaw/
openclaw-node/
*openclaw*.cmd
*openclaw*.ps1

# Local scratch and preview scaffolding. Anything used to run the apps against
# fake data belongs outside a commit — it is not the real schema and must never
# be mistaken for it.
scratch/
scratchpad/
*.preview.mjs
preview-api.mjs
start-preview.sh
.extract-design-system/

# Vercel
.vercel

# Supabase local
supabase/.temp/
supabase/.branches/

# Deno
deno.lock

# Generated by the report preview test (REPORT_PREVIEW=1); never a source file.
report-preview.pdf

# pnpm's local content-addressable store, if it ends up inside the repo
.pnpm-store/

# Test-run artifacts
test-results/
playwright-report/
*.timestamp-*.mjs

# Built installers and the auto-updater manifests beside them. `release/` above
# catches the normal build; these catch an installer copied somewhere else on
# the way to handing it to the lab.
*.exe
*.blockmap
latest*.yml

# Editor and merge leftovers
.vs/
.history/
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*.tmp

# Data pulled out of the database for a one-off. Every one of these is real
# patient data — a name, a phone number, a result — and none of it is source.
exports/
*-export.csv
patient-export*.*
